BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LILT Performance Art Festival\, Day 1: May 13\, 2026
DTSTART:20260513T150000
DTEND:20260513T150000
UID:b3ccaa3cbce9e40165bb3b938a83320b@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the opening day of LILT Festival 2026\, a performa
 nce art festival centring neurodivergent artists. LILT Festival — Day 1 
 May 13\, 3:00–7:10 PM | Gallery TPW Click here to view Artist lineup and
  schedule ​Join us for the opening day of LILT Festival 2026\, a perform
 ance art festival centring neurodivergent artists. Day 1 features a series
  of live works that audiences are welcome to move through at their own pac
 e. LILT Festival includes artistic nudity\, burlesque/stripping\, mature t
 hemes\, and content that may not be suitable for minors. This event is 18+
  Valid ID may be requested at the door. In a moment when performance art i
 s being cut\, underfunded\, and pushed to the margins\, showing up matters
 . Buying a ticket to LILT Festival 2026 directly supports neurodivergent p
 erformance artists creating urgent\, experimental\, and necessary live wor
 k. ​Tickets are available now on a sliding scale from $1- $20 CAD. All p
 roceeds from ticket sales will go directly to the presenting artists. ​T
 his is a ticketed private event. Guests without a ticket will not be permi
 tted to enter\, as required by the venue. Please email contact@lilt.ca if 
 you need assistance securing tickets. ​Visitors are invited to come and 
 go quietly\, spend time with the works\, and engage with each performance 
 on their own terms. ​View the full festival program here: https://files.
 lilt.ca/lilt-festival-2026.pdf ‍
LOCATION:Gallery TPW\, 170 Saint Helens Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/lilt-performance-art-festival-day-1-may-13
 -2026
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:IABC/Toronto Pride Social
DTSTART:20260513T180000
DTEND:20260513T180000
UID:d2c9a144e7ac7166a0cf3a998b9f061f@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Pride is many things: a protest\, a celebration and an opportu
 nity for communicators to reflect on how we show up in authentic solidarit
 y with 2SLGBTQ+ communities through our work. Join IABC/Toronto for an eve
 ning of connection\, conversation and celebration as we gather ahead of Pr
 ide month. Come dressed in your colourful best for an evening with fellow 
 professional communicators in a welcoming\, vibrant space. Panel: A chance
  to learn and ask all those not-so-silly questions! Panelists: Eli Carmona
 \, Communications Specialist at The 519\, Dane Griffiths\, Media Relations
  Advisor at Toronto Public Health and Andrea Houston\, Managing Editor at 
 Ricochet Media. Moderator: Zaina Meher Kadiri\, Senior Communications Coor
 dinator at Pro Bono Ontario We’ll talk about authentic 2SLGBTQ+ represen
 tation\, identifying and avoiding pinkwashing\, the impact of AI on 2SLGBT
 Q+ issues and practical takeaways for Pride and year-round comms campaigns
 . Support a local trans-owned business: Enjoy coffee\, snacks and alcoholi
 c drinks (all for purchase). Learn what’s on at IABC/Toronto: Join our u
 pcoming events and the 2026 IABC World Conference. Questions or access nee
 ds? Email: toronto-idea@iabc.to Fees: • $15: IABC/Toronto professional m
 embers ($16.95 with HST) • $20: IABC Lite members ($22.60 with HST) • 
 $30: Non-members ($33.90 with HST) Spots are limited. Register here Thanks
  to our venue partner Understory for supporting this important conversatio
 n. ‍
LOCATION:Understory Cafe\, 505 Church St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/iabc-toronto-pride-social
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
