BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talk Tea with PolyaMarla: A Queer non-monogamy support group
DTSTART:20260524T180000
DTEND:20260524T180000
UID:efc2ecff8f1b8d2d6e1a6207d498be11@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Get cozy and chat non-monogamy in Queer community! Sip your te
 a\, and grow your heart three sizes. Defying the status quo and queering r
 elationships on our own can be overwhelming. After spending the last few y
 ears focused on online programming\, the PolyaMarla team wanted to create 
 a monthly space to step away from screens\, and build non-monogamous commu
 nity IRL. As facilitators\, we bring a therapeutic background and over fou
 r decades of combined experience practicing non-monogamy. Whether you’ve
  never practiced non-monogamy before\, have been at it for years\, or anyt
 hing in between\, we welcome your perspective. Let’s share non-judgmenta
 l space in the form of casual conversation amongst peers. Bring your curio
 sity\, a cozy sweater\, and let’s spill the hottest tea. About your faci
 litators: Marla (they/them) is a Queer\, gender-defiant\, therapist\, educ
 ator\, and author who specializes in non-monogamous relationships. They ha
 ve been practising polyamory for over 20 years with Adam\, and most recent
 ly published the book Nonmonogamy and Defying a Paradigm. You can catch th
 eir vibe on social media @polyamarla. Adam (he/him) is a bi/Queer creative
  wizard who has been practicing polyamory and producing community-centered
  events at the intersections of culture\, media\, and education since 2005
 . In 2017\, he co-founded EMBRACE: Toronto’s longest-running Queer &amp\
 ; Trans Open Mic. From 2018–2019\, he co-founded LovePlus Collective wit
 h Marla — a monthly non-monogamy peer support group\, and the spiritual 
 predecessor to Talk Tea. * Please note: while Marla is a therapist\, this 
 support group is NOT therapy or a replacement for therapy. ** This is an a
 nti-oppressive\, anti-racist\, and inclusive space for all folx identifyin
 g under the 2SLGBTQIAP+ umbrella. *** Accessibility: Bampot House is unfor
 tunately not wheelchair accessible. There are three steps up the entrance 
 (and a fairly steep ramp)\, as well as 25 steps to enter the back room whe
 re we will be meeting\, which includes a hallway with two steps up and thr
 ee steps down. There are two gender neutral washrooms on site. Bampot Hous
 e is not a scent-free space. There are discounted tickets available for th
 ose with financial constraints. Please contact events@polyamarla.com to in
 quire. Please email us with any accessibility concerns\, and we’ll do ou
 r best to accommodate. ‍
LOCATION:Bampot\, 201 Harbord St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/talk-tea-with-polyamarla-a-queer-non-monog
 amy-support-group
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
